From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:08:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 178/182] fix(gastown): make the Dolt operational-awareness
 fragment city-generic and fail closed on an unknown endpoint (gcp-eqt3d)

The shared operational-awareness fragment is injected into every role card of
every city, but it carried one city's literals: rig:gascity-packs, rig:winnow,
127.0.0.1:3307 and 127.0.0.1:51160 in the doctor example, "load ~20-37",
"6-database city" and "96s on this city" in the measurements. Upstream #265's
test pinned only "port 3307", so none of that tripped it. Separately, diagnostic
step 0 hardcoded DOLT_HOST=127.0.0.1 and carried on with an empty or "null"
port when dolt-state.json or the scope config was unreadable, so every later
step dialled a probe of nothing. That broke upstream #382's rule in the same
file: report the endpoint as unknown and stop, never fall back to a default.

The literals become placeholders (<managed-port>, <inheriting-rig>,
<pinned-rig>, <host>:<external-port>) and the measurements say "under load" or
"~100s on one city", which keeps the 6x headroom arithmetic true. Step 0 now
clears host and port first, resolves them by a case on gc.endpoint_origin
(explicit reads dolt.host/dolt.port; managed_city and inherited_city read the
port from dolt-state.json and claim 127.0.0.1 only once a port exists), and
stops with `return 1 2>/dev/null || exit 1` when either is empty or null. An
unreadable or unrecognised origin also stops now; before, it fell through to
the managed server, which was the default-endpoint fallback the fragment
forbids. Every registered rig and the city carry the key, so no real scope
loses the diagnostic.

Tests: test_prime_prompts_are_city_generic_and_compact now rejects each removed
literal. The new test_operational_awareness_step0_fails_closed extracts step 0
from the shipped fragment, renders {{ .CityRoot }} to a temp city, and runs
each stop case both one-shot and sourced (the sourced shell must survive),
plus the positive managed_city, inherited_city and explicit cases.

Applied verbatim from the design on the bead; both files are pinned by sha256.
patches/ is regenerated into the same commit (docs/fork-patches.md).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../operational-awareness.template.md         |  46 +++++--
 gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh     | 117 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gastown/template-fragments/operational-awareness.template.md b/gastown/template-fragments/operational-awareness.template.md
index d44cbe26..f3a3d02b 100644
--- a/gastown/template-fragments/operational-awareness.template.md
+++ b/gastown/template-fragments/operational-awareness.template.md
@@ -96,9 +96,9 @@ busy city) — give it room rather than assuming it hung.
 gc doctor --json \
   | jq -r '.. | objects | select((.name? // "") | test("dolt-server"))
            | "\(.name) | \(.status) | \(.message)"'
-# dolt-server                   | ok | reachable on 127.0.0.1:51160
-# rig:gascity-packs:dolt-server | ok | inherits city dolt endpoint
-# rig:winnow:dolt-server        | ok | reachable on 127.0.0.1:3307
+# dolt-server                       | ok | reachable on 127.0.0.1:<managed-port>
+# rig:<inheriting-rig>:dolt-server  | ok | inherits city dolt endpoint
+# rig:<pinned-rig>:dolt-server      | ok | reachable on <host>:<external-port>
 ```
 
 Two distinct servers, one of them holding exactly one rig's beads, is a normal
@@ -190,15 +190,35 @@ ts=$(date +%s)
 # 0. Resolve the endpoint for the scope you are investigating and probe THAT
 #    server — this is the resolution the endpoint-origin table above
 #    describes, applied rather than assumed. Run from the rig (or city)
-#    directory whose beads you are chasing.
+#    directory whose beads you are chasing, and run this step with every step
+#    below it as ONE command: the variables it sets are what they dial.
+#    It fails closed. A host or port it cannot resolve, or an origin it cannot
+#    read, leaves the endpoint unknown, and an unknown endpoint ends the run
+#    here; there is no default endpoint to fall back to.
 CFG=.beads/config.yaml
+# Cleared first, so a value left in this shell by an earlier run against another
+# scope cannot stand in for an endpoint this run failed to resolve.
+DOLT_HOST=
+DOLT_PORT=
 ORIGIN=$(grep -E '^[[:space:]]*gc\.endpoint_origin:' "$CFG" | head -1 | sed 's/.*: *//')
-if [ "$ORIGIN" = "explicit" ]; then
-  DOLT_HOST=$(grep -E '^[[:space:]]*dolt\.host:' "$CFG" | head -1 | sed 's/.*: *//')
-  DOLT_PORT=$(grep -E '^[[:space:]]*dolt\.port:' "$CFG" | head -1 | sed 's/.*: *//')
-else
-  DOLT_HOST=127.0.0.1
-  DOLT_PORT=$(jq -r '.port' {{ .CityRoot }}/.gc/runtime/packs/dolt/dolt-state.json)
+case "$ORIGIN" in
+  explicit)
+    DOLT_HOST=$(grep -E '^[[:space:]]*dolt\.host:' "$CFG" | head -1 | sed 's/.*: *//')
+    DOLT_PORT=$(grep -E '^[[:space:]]*dolt\.port:' "$CFG" | head -1 | sed 's/.*: *//')
+    ;;
+  managed_city|inherited_city)
+    # The managed server listens on 127.0.0.1; only its port varies, so the
+    # host is claimed only once dolt-state.json has given a port.
+    DOLT_PORT=$(jq -r '.port' {{ .CityRoot }}/.gc/runtime/packs/dolt/dolt-state.json)
+    case "$DOLT_PORT" in ''|null) ;; *) DOLT_HOST=127.0.0.1 ;; esac
+    ;;
+esac
+if [ -z "$DOLT_HOST" ] || [ "$DOLT_HOST" = null ] || [ -z "$DOLT_PORT" ] || [ "$DOLT_PORT" = null ]; then
+  printf 'diagnostic: endpoint is unknown for scope %s (gc.endpoint_origin: %s, host: %s, port: %s); report that and stop. Run no later step, and do not fall back to any default endpoint.\n' \
+    "$PWD" "${ORIGIN:-unreadable}" "${DOLT_HOST:-unresolved}" "${DOLT_PORT:-unresolved}" >&2
+  # `return` ends a sourced block and leaves the sourcing shell alive; run as
+  # a one-shot command there is nothing to return from, and `exit` ends it.
+  return 1 2>/dev/null || exit 1
 fi
 echo "probing ${ORIGIN:-unknown} endpoint ${DOLT_HOST}:${DOLT_PORT}"
 # Dolt 2.x has no `sql-client` subcommand: the connection flags are GLOBAL and
@@ -209,7 +229,7 @@ echo "probing ${ORIGIN:-unknown} endpoint ${DOLT_HOST}:${DOLT_PORT}"
 # 1. Capture live process state via SQL (non-fatal — Dolt keeps running).
 #    SHOW FULL PROCESSLIST lists active connections, the query each is
 #    running, and time-in-state. Straight at the endpoint it costs 0.10-0.31s
-#    (measured, load ~20-37), so a 10s wall is ~30x headroom: if this one
+#    (measured under load), so a 10s wall is ~30x headroom: if this one
 #    fires, the server genuinely is not answering.
 run_bounded 10 dolt --host "$DOLT_HOST" --port "$DOLT_PORT" \
       --user "${DOLT_USER:-root}" --password "${DOLT_PASSWORD:-}" --no-tls \
@@ -231,7 +251,7 @@ cat /tmp/dolt-hang-$ts-logs.log
 
 # 3. Capture the structured health snapshot — the one managed-server view with
 #    no direct-SQL equivalent, since it knows which databases the city expects.
-#    Measured 8.2-24.3s on a 6-database city at load ~20-37 (it bounds each
+#    Measured 8.2-24.3s on a multi-database city under load (it bounds each
 #    per-database probe internally with `run_bounded 5`, then pays gc's startup
 #    on top). 60s is ~2.5x that worst case; if it fires, treat it as evidence
 #    the data plane is wedged and escalate.
@@ -262,7 +282,7 @@ cat /tmp/dolt-hang-$ts-status.log
 
 # 5. Probe every rig's OWN endpoint, including externally-pinned ones the steps
 #    above only cover when you happen to be standing in that rig. gc doctor
-#    walks every rig and is slow — measured 96s on this city, and it grows with
+#    walks every rig and is slow — measured ~100s on one city, and it grows with
 #    rig count, so 600s is ~6x headroom. Treat a timeout here as a finding, not
 #    as permission to skip the step.
 run_bounded 600 gc doctor --json > /tmp/dolt-hang-$ts-doctor.json 2>&1
diff --git a/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh b/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
index 40f32f53..2a9d11bc 100755
--- a/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
+++ b/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
@@ -843,6 +843,18 @@ test_prime_prompts_are_city_generic_and_compact() {
         fail "operational awareness must require configured and probed endpoint evidence"
     grep -F 'endpoint is unknown and stop' "$awareness" >/dev/null ||
         fail "operational awareness must fail closed when endpoint discovery fails"
+    # gcp-eqt3d: the fragment is injected into every role card of every city, so
+    # an example lifted from one city's `gc doctor` output or one measurement
+    # run teaches that city's rig names, ports and load as if they were the
+    # schema. These are the literals that were there; the teaching they carried
+    # (an inheriting rig, an externally pinned rig, a measured headroom) is
+    # kept with placeholders.
+    local literal
+    for literal in 'rig:gascity-packs' 'rig:winnow' '127.0.0.1:3307' '127.0.0.1:51160' \
+        '96s on this city' '6-database city' 'load ~20-37'; do
+        ! grep -F -- "$literal" "$awareness" >/dev/null ||
+            fail "operational awareness must stay city-generic; it still carries the city-specific literal '$literal'"
+    done
     grep -F 'run_bounded() {' "$awareness" >/dev/null ||
         fail "operational awareness should define a portable diagnostic timeout helper"
     # Steps 1 and 4 dial the resolved endpoint directly, not through `gc`:
@@ -1336,6 +1348,110 @@ $hits"
     done
 }
 
+# gcp-eqt3d: the fragment says "If endpoint discovery fails, report that the
+# endpoint is unknown and stop; never fall back to any default endpoint", and
+# step 0 is the only place that rule can be executed. It used to hardcode the
+# managed host and carry on with an empty or "null" host/port when
+# dolt-state.json or the scope's config could not be read, so every later step
+# dialled `--host 127.0.0.1 --port ` (or `--port null`): a probe of nothing,
+# presented as a measurement of the scope under investigation. Extract the
+# shipped step and run it, because a content grep cannot see that the guard
+# fires, only that it was typed.
+test_operational_awareness_step0_fails_closed() {
+    local awareness block city scope out rc
+    awareness="$GASTOWN/template-fragments/operational-awareness.template.md"
+    command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail "jq is required (step 0 of the shipped bundle uses it)"
+
+    STEP0_TMP=$(mktemp -d)
+    trap 'rm -rf "$STEP0_TMP"' EXIT
+    city="$STEP0_TMP/city"
+    scope="$STEP0_TMP/scope"
+    block="$STEP0_TMP/step0.sh"
+    mkdir -p "$city/.gc/runtime/packs/dolt" "$scope/.beads"
+
+    # The block is the lines from the step 0 header up to (not including) the
+    # step 1 header. Its one template action is the city root, rendered here to
+    # the temp city; any other action would be an unrendered literal.
+    sed -n '/^# 0\. Resolve the endpoint/,/^# 1\. Capture/p' "$awareness" |
+        sed '$d' |
+        sed "s|{{ \.CityRoot }}|$city|g" >"$block"
+    [[ -s "$block" ]] ||
+        fail "step 0 not found between '# 0. Resolve the endpoint' and '# 1. Capture'"
+    grep -F 'DOLT_PORT' "$block" >/dev/null ||
+        fail "step 0 extraction came back without the endpoint resolution"
+    ! grep -F '# 1. Capture' "$block" >/dev/null ||
+        fail "step 0 extraction overshot its '# 1. Capture' anchor"
+    ! grep -F '{{' "$block" >/dev/null ||
+        fail "step 0 carries a template action the test does not render: $(grep -F '{{' "$block")"
+
+    # step0_run <env assignments...>: run the block from the scope dir the way
+    # an agent's one-shot Bash call does. rc and merged output come back in
+    # $rc and $out; a second run SOURCES it in a shell that must outlive it.
+    step0_run() {
+        rc=0
+        out=$(cd "$scope" && env "$@" bash "$block" 2>&1) || rc=$?
+    }
+    expect_stop() {
+        local label="$1" src
+        [[ "$rc" -ne 0 ]] ||
+            fail "step 0 ($label) must stop with a non-zero status, got 0: $out"
+        [[ "$out" == *'endpoint is unknown'* ]] ||
+            fail "step 0 ($label) must print 'endpoint is unknown': $out"
+        [[ "$out" != *probing* ]] ||
+            fail "step 0 ($label) went on to probe an endpoint it did not resolve: $out"
+        # An agent that sources the block must keep its shell: return, not exit.
+        src=$(cd "$scope" && bash -c 'source "$1"; echo SHELL-SURVIVED' _ "$block" 2>&1) || true
+        [[ "$src" == *'endpoint is unknown'* && "$src" == *SHELL-SURVIVED* && "$src" != *probing* ]] ||
+            fail "step 0 ($label) must stop a sourced block without killing the shell: $src"
+    }
+
+    # (a) managed_city, no dolt-state.json.
+    printf 'gc.endpoint_origin: managed_city\n' >"$scope/.beads/config.yaml"
+    rm -f "$city/.gc/runtime/packs/dolt/dolt-state.json"
+    step0_run
+    expect_stop "managed_city, no dolt-state.json"
+
+    # (a') dolt-state.json readable but carrying no port: jq prints the literal
+    # string null, which is not an empty string and used to sail through.
+    printf '{"running":true}\n' >"$city/.gc/runtime/packs/dolt/dolt-state.json"
+    step0_run
+    expect_stop "managed_city, dolt-state.json without a port"
+
+    # (b) explicit with a host and no port, and the mirror image.
+    printf 'gc.endpoint_origin: explicit\ndolt.host: 10.0.0.5\n' >"$scope/.beads/config.yaml"
+    step0_run
+    expect_stop "explicit, dolt.host only"
+    printf 'gc.endpoint_origin: explicit\ndolt.port: 3306\n' >"$scope/.beads/config.yaml"
+    step0_run
+    expect_stop "explicit, dolt.port only"
+
+    # (d) the scope's config unreadable: the origin is then unknown, and an
+    # unknown origin must not be read as "the managed server" (that is a default
+    # endpoint). A value left in the shell by an earlier run against another
+    # scope must not stand in for the one this run failed to resolve either.
+    printf '{"port":51160}\n' >"$city/.gc/runtime/packs/dolt/dolt-state.json"
+    rm -f "$scope/.beads/config.yaml"
+    step0_run DOLT_HOST=10.9.9.9 DOLT_PORT=9999
+    expect_stop "no .beads/config.yaml, stale DOLT_HOST/DOLT_PORT in the environment"
+
+    # (c) the resolved cases still go through, with the endpoint they resolved.
+    printf 'gc.endpoint_origin: managed_city\n' >"$scope/.beads/config.yaml"
+    step0_run
+    [[ "$rc" -eq 0 ]] || fail "step 0 (managed_city with a port) must succeed, rc=$rc: $out"
+    [[ "$out" == *'probing managed_city endpoint 127.0.0.1:51160'* ]] ||
+        fail "step 0 must probe the port dolt-state.json names for managed_city: $out"
+    [[ "$out" != *'endpoint is unknown'* ]] ||
+        fail "step 0 resolved an endpoint and still called it unknown: $out"
+    printf 'gc.endpoint_origin: inherited_city\n' >"$scope/.beads/config.yaml"
+    step0_run
+    [[ "$rc" -eq 0 && "$out" == *'probing inherited_city endpoint 127.0.0.1:51160'* ]] ||
+        fail "step 0 (inherited_city) must resolve the managed server's port, rc=$rc: $out"
+    printf 'gc.endpoint_origin: explicit\ndolt.host: 10.0.0.5\ndolt.port: 3306\n' >"$scope/.beads/config.yaml"
+    step0_run
+    [[ "$rc" -eq 0 && "$out" == *'probing explicit endpoint 10.0.0.5:3306'* ]] ||
+        fail "step 0 (explicit) must resolve the pinned host:port from the scope config, rc=$rc: $out"
+}
+
 test_dog_assets_are_pack_local
 test_retired_dog_formulas_are_not_reintroduced
 test_work_bead_is_never_claimed
@@ -1354,6 +1470,7 @@ test_claim_decline_writes_nothing_on_any_bead
 test_polecat_claim_ships_as_a_script_not_a_heredoc
 test_review_leg_contract_forbids_synthetic_mutation
 test_prime_prompts_are_city_generic_and_compact
+test_operational_awareness_step0_fails_closed
 test_witness_wisp_queries_pin_include_infra
 test_witness_handoff_recovery_is_guarded_and_fail_closed
 test_boot_wisp_queries_pin_include_infra
